<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσία</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Asia,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.4
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				4.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				412
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ Ἀσία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					694
				</span></i>
			, etc.:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιᾱνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<i>Asian, Asiatic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.6
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀ. ῥήτορες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theon
					<u>Prog.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀ. ζῆλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					14.1.41
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς, ἑστιᾶν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					46.30
				</span></i>
			:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span> [the latter with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span>], freq. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>, never in <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιάς</span> being required by
			the metre in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1397
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1168
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσίς</span> in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				270
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				547
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				34
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιάς</span> (sc.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				748
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ion</u>
				1356
			</span></i>; also (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιθάρα</span>), <i>the
				Asian harp,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				120
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1133c
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιάτης</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσθμ-ᾶτις</span></b> , 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσθμ-ήτης</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσθμ-ῆτις</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				61
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, etc.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσιᾱτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				15.2.8
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσίηθεν</span></b> ,
				Adv.
			<i>from Asia</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				6336
			</span></i>. (Fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσιος</span> (q.
		v.).)</div>
